# Copy to .env.local to override. Every value has a working default, so the app
# runs against a local API with no configuration at all.

# Base URL of the calculation API. Same-origin by default: Vite proxies /v1 in
# development and nginx proxies it in the container, so nothing is ever
# cross-origin and CORS never applies.
# VITE_API_URL=/v1

# Where the dev-server proxy forwards /v1. Build-time only, read by vite.config.ts.
# VITE_API_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# ⚠️ These ship inside the JavaScript bundle and are readable by any user. That
# is inherent to a browser SPA, not an oversight: the token buys per-client
# attribution, while the real defence is the API's rate limiting, CORS
# allowlist and payload caps. Never put a production secret here.
# VITE_API_CLIENT_ID=web
# VITE_API_CLIENT_SECRET=dev-secret
